---
title: "Board releases: validate, drain, switch, recover"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: Previous release serving
  s1: Candidate prepared away from active code
  s2: Deployment refused or previous release restored
  s3: Code, assets, config and schema checked
  s4: Previous code retained
  s5: Store quiet#59; ready to drain
  s6: Previous process exited
  s7: No process running#59; restoring previous pointer
  s8: Final store saved beside retained code
  s9: Previous code selected#59; ready for manual manager
  s10: Current release switched with no process running
  s11: Candidate running#59; checking health
  s12: Candidate accepted
  s13: Failed candidate must exit before restoration
  s14: Stop timed out#59; journal retained for manual recovery
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: prepare candidate
  s1 --> s2: reject invalid code or unsupported store schema
  s1 --> s3: accept candidate checks
  s3 --> s4: retain previous code without overwriting it
  s3 --> s2: fault or quiet/stop timeout#59; leave previous process alone
  s4 --> s2: fault or quiet/stop timeout#59; leave previous process alone
  s4 --> s5: wait until store is quiet
  s5 --> s2: fault or quiet/stop timeout#59; leave previous process alone
  s5 --> s6: stop and flush previous process
  s6 --> s7: fault or failed startup#59; enter restoration
  s6 --> s8: save final store safety copy
  s7 --> s9: restore retained previous release
  s8 --> s7: fault or failed startup#59; enter restoration
  s8 --> s10: atomically rename current release link
  s9 --> s2: start previous release#59; report deployment failure
  s10 --> s11: start pinned candidate path
  s10 --> s7: fault or failed startup#59; enter restoration
  s11 --> s12: accept running process, HTTP 200, cards and clean log
  s11 --> s13: reject health check
  s13 --> s7: confirm candidate process exited
  s13 --> s14: refuse switch while candidate still runs
